    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead reveal">Corporate sustainability across Asia-Pacific is no longer a discretionary corporate social responsibility exercise. It is a core operational priority.</p>
      <p class="reveal">Yet, the region faces a reality check. As our recent research in <a href="http://bt.sg/poweringasean2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Powering Asean’s Future 2026</a> shows, South-east Asia stands at a juncture. Sustainability is running headlong into short-term financial pressures and compressed margins and rising energy costs are forcing many companies to delay their decarbonisation targets.</p>
      <p class="reveal">The transition itself has not stopped. We see this persistence and recognise it annually through our Sustainability Impact Awards, organised by <i>The Business Times</i> and UOB, with the Centre for Governance and Sustainability (CGS) at NUS Business School as ourknowledge partner.</p>
      <p class="reveal">We now want to take that evaluation a step further. <i>The Business Times has</i> partnered CGS to launch the Asia Pacific Sustainability Index (APSI).</p>
      <p class="reveal">Evaluating corporate disclosure across 14 distinct markets, which span mature regulatory regimes to emerging markets with phased guidelines, presents a genuine challenge for investors and business leaders.</p>
      <p class="reveal">The APSI addresses this through a contextualised methodology. It evaluates 700 listed companies against the MAGNET framework to determine a base score, then applies a context factor to account for local regulatory requirements. This separates a company’s actual disclosure quality from its jurisdiction-wide mandates.</p>
      <p class="reveal">The findings establish a clear baseline: sustainability reporting has achieved scale across Asia Pacific, but depth remains uneven. While broad emissions pledges are common, substantive board oversight, detailed climate scenario modeling, and credible Scope 3 accounting remain scarce.</p>
      <p class="reveal">We hope this index serves as a clear, unvarnished guide for tracking progress in regional corporate transparency.</p>
      <p class="signoff reveal"><b>Mindy Tan</b><span>BT Insights Editor</span></p>
